<title>SWITZERLAND: Valora plans share payback of 15 Sfrs.</title>
<headline>Valora plans share payback of 15 Sfrs.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss-based retail group Valora Holding AG said that it planned to pay back 15 Swiss francs per share to shareholders to reduce capital, providing it receives their approval at its annual meeting.</p>
<p>It said it was also proposing a dividend of six francs per share on its results for the 1996 business year, which it said represented a 20 percent increase.</p>
<p>It also said that sales in the first four months of 1997 rose 5.4 percent.</p>
<p>It said that strict cost controls were expected to allow it to further improve profitability in the current year. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
